In article <1991Jun3.202153.1652@dayton.saic.com> user_442@dayton.saic.com writes:
>
>In regards to wishing for other things, I recently (January or February) read
>about 10 sheets of paper entitled Nethack Spoilers.  In that marvelous tome
>there were many suggestions as to useful things to wish for (almost all of
>which I concur whole heartedly.
>
>Some of these are:
>
>blessed +3 war hammer named Mjollnir

In this case, go for +2.  The reason is that two blessed enchant
weapon scrolls will run the hammer up to +8 safely, since it is
safe to enchant further from +5.  If you start at +3, you have
a problem.  As an added benefit, you are less likely to be turned
down for a +2 enchantment.

>blessed +3 broad sword named Stormbringer
>blessed +3 long sword named Excaliber (or is it Excalibre? :( )

Actually, its Excalibur.  OK to go for the +3 enchantment here,
because you can run a sword down one level by engraving a two letter
engraving in the floor.  So get it and use it at +3, then +6, but
when you get one more blessed enchant weapon scroll, take it down
to +5 first.
>
>...
>blessed +3 boots of speed (or jumping if you are already speeded)
                            ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
No, no! Intrinsic speed (obtained by zapping yourself with a wand
of speed monster, among other ways) gives you an extra move about
a third of the time.  Speed boots double your speed vs. normal.
As I have stated before: properly used, these are the most powerful
items in the game, and should be your first wish.
(well...actually, your first wish on a wand would be a blessed scroll of
charging...)

>[ other suggestions deleted]

Typically a second wish will be for the gray dragon scale mail.
Blessed luckstones are also quite nice.   As for Mjollnir, Stormy,
etc., I try to get them at altars.  The helm of opposite alignment
is VERY handy for non-chaotic characters in hell.


